==Dutch==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nl|/ʋaːr/}}
* {{audio|nl|Nl-waar.ogg|audio}}
* {{hyphenation|nl|waar}}
* {{rhymes|nl|aːr}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|nl|ine-pro|*kʷ-}}
From {{inh|nl|dum|wāer}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|*war}}, from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*hwar}}. Cognate with {{cog|en|where}}.

====Adverb====
{{nl-adv}}

# {{lb|nl|interrogative}} [[where]], in which place
#: {{ux|nl|'''Waar''' is Jan?|'''Where''' is John?}}
# {{lb|nl|relative}} [[where]], the place that
#: {{ux|nl|Dit is '''waar''' hij woont.|This is '''where''' he lives.}}
# {{lb|nl|interrogative|with a preposition}} [[what]], which thing
#: {{ux|nl|'''Waar''' is dat goed voor?|'''What''' is that good for?}}
# {{lb|nl|relative|with a preposition}} [[what]], that which
#: {{ux|nl|Dit is '''waar''' dat goed voor is.|This is '''what''' that is good for.}}

=====Usage notes=====
With a preposition, {{m|nl||waar}} is used instead of {{m|nl|wat}} to create a [[pronominal adverb]]. See also [[:Category:Dutch pronominal adverbs]].

=====Derived terms=====
See [[:Category:Dutch pronominal adverbs]]

